{"ruling":{"ruling":"FULL_REFUND","amount_sgd":6.0,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"referrals":[],"confidence":0.95,"explanation":"To the rider: your claim is supported, and the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee is refunded to you in full. On the platform's own records all three limbs of POL-NS-04 hold. Limb (a): the chat log shows two messages from you inside the waiting window that are squarely locating and coordinating - 'I am at Exit D under the green sign. Where is your car?' at 18:21:00 and 'I still cannot see you. Please reply.' at 18:23:25. Limb (b): the driver posted no reply at all - the chat log's three entries are one system notice and your two messages - and trip_record.in_app_calls is an empty array, so no voice call was placed either; the first message even carries a read receipt at 18:21:15, so the driver saw the request and let the 120 second window pass. Limb (c): your device sat 41.9 m from the pickup pin on 16 of 16 qualifying fixes, well inside the 200 m presence radius for a TRANSPORT_HUB and stationary throughout. This is the affirmatively-satisfied case, not the 'undecidable and neutral' case the clause reserves for an absent rider_track. POL-NS-04 is one of the clauses POL-NS-01 expressly yields to ('no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces them'), so it displaces the charge.

To the driver: your account that you waited inside the station geofence until the timer ended is consistent with the trace and I have accepted it. The four limbs of POL-NS-01 are indeed made out - an 'arrived' event at 18:20:20; the trace placing you 24.0 m from the pin, inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius; a continuous in-geofence dwell of 330 seconds from 18:20:00 to 18:25:30 against the 300 second minimum; and termination by you at 18:25:30 on RIDER_NO_SHOW after the dwell elapsed. The arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05 (0 km/h, 24 m from the pin), and there is no shortfall to open POL-NS-06 (a 30 second surplus). But POL-NS-01 makes a no-show fee chargeable only where no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-04 does displace it on these facts. POL-NS-07 compensates at 80 percent only where POL-NS-01 stands undisplaced, so the payout you claimed (SGD 4.80) is not payable here, and the anti-farming check you addressed correctly does not fire either way. The fee line of SGD 6.00 reconciles with the fee schedule's resolution rule (TRANSPORT_HUB zone-class fee SGD 6.00 and RYDE_PLUS vehicle-tier fee SGD 6.00 tie, so the greater is SGD 6.00), so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged.

On integrity and escalation: every artifact that carries a deciding fact - the GPS trace, the trip record and the chat log - was admitted COMPLETE at weight 1.0, and the traces show no gap over 120 seconds, 34 fixes across the window and a rider track present. No limb (a) to (d) of POL-NS-08 is engaged, so nothing down-weights the ruling. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no two artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence, both parties' disputes_with_counterparty_90d read 0, the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (1 termination in 30 days against 120 completed trips), and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0. The MISSING traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09106-01, weight 0.0) is relied on by no part of the outcome: POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is not needed because there was a single continuous in-geofence run that already met the minimum. No clause produces a referral in this case, so none is issued. The disputed amount moves to you, the filing party, as a FULL_REFUND."},"discarded_claims":[]}

