    "explanation": "Rider — you get the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee back, and the driver receives no compensation.\n\nThe driver's account of the baseline test is largely correct, and I accept it. POL-NS-01 is made out on its face: the trip record carries an 'arrived' event at 18:20:20 (limb a); the GPS trace puts the driver about 24 m from the pickup pin, well inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius, from 18:20:00, i.e. before that event (limb b); he held position for one continuous in-geofence run of 330 seconds against the 300-second TRANSPORT_HUB minimum, a 30-second surplus (limb c); and there is no boarding event and the trip was terminated by the driver at 18:25:30 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the dwell had elapsed (limb d). I also accept the driver's POL-NS-02 (geofence), POL-NS-05 (the arrival marker was true — 24 m from the pin at 0 km/h), POL-NS-06 (no shortfall to refund) and POL-NS-03 (this is not a wrong-entrance case; his stationary fixes were inside the arrival radius) points. None of that decides the case, because POL-NS-01 chargeability is expressly 'where all four conditions hold and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces them'.\n\nPOL-NS-04 does displace it. Its three limbs are all satisfied on the platform's own records. Limb (a): the chat log shows the rider sent locating/coordinating messages inside the waiting window — 'I am at Exit D under the green sign. Where is your car?' at 18:21:00 and 'I still cannot see you. Please reply.' at 18:23:25 — each stating her position and asking for the driver's. Limb (b): there is no driver-side chat entry at all, and trip_record.in_app_calls is an empty array, so the driver neither replied within 120 seconds of either message nor placed an in-app call before terminating the trip; the first message carries a read receipt 15 seconds after it was sent, so the request was seen, not merely sent. Limb (c): all 16 of the rider's qualifying GPS fixes sit about 41.9 m from the pin, inside the 200 m TRANSPORT_HUB presence radius, and her device is stationary throughout — this is the affirmatively satisfied case, not the 'undecidable and neutral' one the clause reserves for a missing rider track. All three limbs hold, so the rider is exonerated: the fee is refunded in full, with no driver compensation payable. The driver's POL-NS-07 claim fails for that reason — POL-NS-07 only operates where POL-NS-01 is satisfied and undisplaced, and POL-NS-04 removes both the charge and the payout. The driver's own submission does not dispute the facts on which the rider's clause turns.\n\nNo escalation and no referral. The disputed line is the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee actually charged (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). Every artifact this ruling rests on — the chat log, the trip record and the GPS trace — is admitted at weight 1.0, so nothing drags confidence down, and the fee line reconciles with the fee schedule (TRANSPORT_HUB 6.00 and RYDE_PLUS 6.00 tie; the greater is 6.00), so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged and no limb (a)–(d) impairment applies. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: both parties' trailing-window and counterparty counters read 0, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (1 no-show termination in 30 days against 120 completed trips). The lifetime counter rider_profile.prior_no_show_flags and the rating/account-age fields are context only under POL-GEN-01 and have been given no weight in either direction."
